# Project Constitution — Nelna FG Digital Recording System

## Purpose

This repository implements a Finished Goods digital recording system. Documentation and code in this repository must support safe, auditable factory-floor recording without inventing business rules or claiming production readiness prematurely.

## Non-negotiable principles

1. Modular monolith only — no microservices in initial delivery.
2. Business logic lives in domain services, not views or templates.
3. Complex reads use selectors/query services.
4. Authorization and separation-of-duty rules use policies; deny by default.
5. Multi-record business operations use database transactions.
6. Preserve operational history; do not destroy submitted or approved records.
7. Corrections use amendments with full before/after history.
8. Critical failures trigger deterministic rules, never AI final decisions.
9. Important operations create audit events.
10. Photos and large files are not stored in PostgreSQL.
11. ERP availability must not be required for factory-floor recording.
12. Do not invent temperature limits, CCP classifications, sites, departments, shifts, products, checklist items, or approval rules.
13. Every business rule must identify its business owner and evidence source.
14. Sinhala support is mandatory for operator-facing content.
15. Operator workflows must minimize typing and be faster than paper in normal use.
16. Production readiness requires UAT, restore testing, security review, and owner approval.

## Approved technical direction

- Python backend, Django 5.2 LTS, PostgreSQL, Redis, Celery
- Django Templates, HTMX, Tailwind CSS, minimal JavaScript, Alpine.js only where needed
- Responsive installable PWA; no native mobile app in initial phases
- MinIO locally; S3-compatible object storage in production
- Pytest and Playwright; GitHub Actions CI
- Local AI (e.g. Ollama) may be added later as assistance only

## Explicit prohibitions

- No secrets in source control
- No shared user accounts
- No direct ERP database writes
- No destructive deletion of operational data
- No production deployment without explicit written approval
- No unsupported compliance claims
- No invented Nelna operational values
- No AI final decisions for food safety, QA, loading release, CAPA closure, or access control
- Do not reuse or copy code from any previous repository

## Delivery control

- Work proceeds phase by phase on dedicated branches with pull requests
- Manual PR review is required before merge
- Phase exit criteria and approval gates must be met before the next phase starts
